    "intro_narrative": "You are a rogue archivist who just boarded the derelict orbital research station 'Aegis-VII'. The station has been drifting in silent space for over a decade following a mysterious, abrupt evacuation. Deep within its labyrinthine corridors lies a highly classified data core, said to contain revolutionary astrophysical research. Your sensors indicate that the prized data is protected by multiple layers of nested physical containment and advanced biometric security measures.\n\nAs you step into the dimly lit maintenance bay, the low hum of failing life support systems echoes around you. Emergency red lights flicker intermittently, casting long, unsettling shadows over forgotten equipment and scattered cargo. Your objective is to explore this decaying facility, utilize any functional tools left behind by the fleeing scientists, and breach the station's ultimate safe. To secure the data core, you must carefully navigate through hidden caches and bypass encrypted locks. The station's automated defenses may be offline, but its cryptographic barriers remain unyielding. Your success depends entirely on your observational skills and deductive reasoning.",
